      "full_name": "taylor_isLittleO",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: taylor_isLittleO | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {E : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] {f : ℝ → E} {x₀ : ℝ} {n : ℕ} {s : Set ℝ},\n  Convex ℝ s →\n    x₀ ∈ s →\n      ContDiffOn ℝ (↑n) f s → (fun x => f x - taylorWithinEval f n s x₀ x) =o[nhdsWithin x₀ s] fun x => (x - x₀) ^ n | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Taylor",
      "informal_statement": "Let $E$ be a normed vector space over $\\mathbb{R}$, $s \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ a convex set containing a point $x_0 \\in s$, and $f : \\mathbb{R} \\to E$ a $C^n$ function on $s$. Then the remainder term of the Taylor approximation satisfies:\n\n\\[\nf(x) - T_n(f, s, x_0)(x) = o((x - x_0)^n) \\quad \\text{as} \\quad x \\to x_0 \\text{ within } s,\n\\]\n\nwhere $T_n(f, s, x_0)(x) = \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{(x - x_0)^k}{k!} f^{(k)}(x_0)$ is the Taylor polynomial of order $n$ for $f$ at $x_0$ within $s$."
    },
    {
      "full_name": "taylor_mean_remainder_bound",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: taylor_mean_remainder_bound | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {E : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] {f : ℝ → E} {a b C x : ℝ} {n : ℕ},\n  a ≤ b →\n    ContDiffOn ℝ (↑n + 1) f (Set.Icc a b) →\n      x ∈ Set.Icc a b →\n        (∀ y ∈ Set.Icc a b, ‖iteratedDerivWithin (n + 1) f (Set.Icc a b) y‖ ≤ C) →\n          ‖f x - taylorWithinEval f n (Set.Icc a b) a x‖ ≤ C * (x - a) ^ (n + 1) / ↑n.factorial | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Taylor",
      "informal_statement": "Let $f \\colon \\mathbb{R} \\to E$ be a function where $E$ is a normed vector space, and let $a \\leq b$ be real numbers. Suppose:\n1. $f$ is $C^{n+1}$ on the closed interval $[a, b]$,\n2. For all $y \\in [a, b]$, the $(n+1)$-th derivative of $f$ within $[a, b]$ satisfies $\\|f^{(n+1)}(y)\\| \\leq C$ for some constant $C \\geq 0$.\n\nThen for any $x \\in [a, b]$, the error between $f(x)$ and its $n$-th degree Taylor polynomial evaluated at $x$ is bounded by:\n\\[\n\\|f(x) - T_n(f, [a, b], a)(x)\\| \\leq C \\cdot \\frac{(x - a)^{n+1}}{n!}.\n\\]"
    },
    {
      "full_name": "exists_taylor_mean_remainder_bound",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: exists_taylor_mean_remainder_bound | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {E : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] {f : ℝ → E} {a b : ℝ} {n : ℕ},\n  a ≤ b →\n    ContDiffOn ℝ (↑n + 1) f (Set.Icc a b) →\n      ∃ C, ∀ x ∈ Set.Icc a b, ‖f x - taylorWithinEval f n (Set.Icc a b) a x‖ ≤ C * (x - a) ^ (n + 1) | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Taylor",
      "informal_statement": "Let $f \\colon \\mathbb{R} \\to E$ be a function where $E$ is a normed vector space, and let $a \\leq b$ be real numbers. If $f$ is $C^{n+1}$ on the closed interval $[a, b]$, then there exists a constant $C \\geq 0$ such that for all $x \\in [a, b]$, the error between $f(x)$ and its $n$-th degree Taylor polynomial evaluated at $x$ satisfies:\n\\[\n\\|f(x) - T_n(f, [a, b], a)(x)\\| \\leq C \\cdot (x - a)^{n+1}.\n\\]"
