    {
      "full_name": "Convex.taylor_approx_two_segment",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: Convex.taylor_approx_two_segment | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {E : Type u_1} {F : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : NormedAddCommGroup F]\n  [inst_3 : NormedSpace ℝ F] {s : Set E},\n  Convex ℝ s →\n    ∀ {f : E → F} {f' : E → E →L[ℝ] F} {f'' : E →L[ℝ] E →L[ℝ] F},\n      (∀ x ∈ interior s, HasFDerivAt f (f' x) x) →\n        ∀ {x : E},\n          x ∈ s →\n            HasFDerivWithinAt f' f'' (interior s) x →\n              ∀ {v w : E},\n                x + v ∈ interior s →\n                  x + v + w ∈ interior s →\n                    (fun h =>\n                        f (x + h • v + h • w) - f (x + h • v) - h • (f' x) w - h ^ 2 • (f'' v) w -\n                          (h ^ 2 / 2) • (f'' w) w) =o[nhdsWithin 0 (Set.Ioi 0)]\n                      fun h => h ^ 2 | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Symmetric",
      "informal_statement": "Let $E$ and $F$ be real normed vector spaces and let $s\\subseteq E$ be a convex set. Suppose $f\\colon E\\to F$ is differentiable on $\\operatorname{interior} s$ with derivative $f'\\colon E\\to E\\toL[ℝ]F$, and that $f'$ is differentiable at a point $x\\in s$ with second derivative $f''\\colon E\\toL[ℝ]E\\toL[ℝ]F$.  For any vectors $v,w\\in E$ such that $x+v$ and $x+v+w$ lie in $\\operatorname{interior} s$, we have\n$$\n f(x+h\\,v+h\\,w)-f(x+h\\,v)-h\\,f'(x)w-h^{2}\\,(f''v)w-\\frac{h^{2}}{2}\\,(f''w)w\n = o(h^{2})\\qquad(h\\to0^{+}).\n$$\nIn other words,\n$$\n f(x+h\\,v+h\\,w)=f(x+h\\,v)+h\\,f'(x)w+h^{2}\\,(f''v)w+\\frac{h^{2}}{2}\\,(f''w)w+o(h^{2})\\quad(h\\to0^{+}).\n$$\nThis gives a bilinear estimate for the increment of $f$ along the segment $[x+hv,\\;x+hv+hw]$ inside $s$."
