    {
      "full_name": "taylor_mean_remainder_lagrange",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: taylor_mean_remainder_lagrange | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {f : ℝ → ℝ} {x x₀ : ℝ} {n : ℕ},\n  x₀ < x →\n    ContDiffOn ℝ (↑n) f (Set.Icc x₀ x) →\n      DifferentiableOn ℝ (iteratedDerivWithin n f (Set.Icc x₀ x)) (Set.Ioo x₀ x) →\n        ∃ x' ∈ Set.Ioo x₀ x,\n          f x - taylorWithinEval f n (Set.Icc x₀ x) x₀ x =\n            iteratedDerivWithin (n + 1) f (Set.Icc x₀ x) x' * (x - x₀) ^ (n + 1) / ↑(n + 1).factorial | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Taylor",
      "informal_statement": "Let $f \\colon \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a function, and let $x_0, x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $x_0 < x$. Suppose that:\n1. $f$ is $n$ times continuously differentiable on the closed interval $[x_0, x]$,\n2. The $n$-th iterated derivative of $f$ within $[x_0, x]$ is differentiable on the open interval $(x_0, x)$.\n\nThen there exists a point $x' \\in (x_0, x)$ such that\n\\[\nf(x) - T_n(f, [x_0, x], x_0)(x) = \\frac{f^{(n+1)}(x') (x - x_0)^{n+1}}{(n+1)!},\n\\]\nwhere $T_n(f, [x_0, x], x_0)(x)$ denotes the Taylor polynomial of degree $n$ for $f$ on $[x_0, x]$ evaluated at $x$, and $f^{(n+1)}(x')$ is the $(n+1)$-th derivative of $f$ at $x'$ within $[x_0, x]$."
    },
    {
      "full_name": "taylor_mean_remainder_lagrange_iteratedDeriv",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: taylor_mean_remainder_lagrange_iteratedDeriv | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {f : ℝ → ℝ} {x x₀ : ℝ} {n : ℕ},\n  x₀ < x →\n    ContDiffOn ℝ (↑n + 1) f (Set.Icc x₀ x) →\n      ∃ x' ∈ Set.Ioo x₀ x,\n        f x - taylorWithinEval f n (Set.Icc x₀ x) x₀ x =\n          iteratedDeriv (n + 1) f x' * (x - x₀) ^ (n + 1) / ↑(n + 1).factorial | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Taylor",
      "informal_statement": "Let $f : \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a function that is $C^{n+1}$ on the closed interval $[x_0,x]$ with $x_0 < x$. Then there exists a point $\\xi \\in (x_0,x)$ such that\\[\\begin{aligned}\\text{f}(x) - T_n(f;[x_0,x],x_0)(x) &= \\operatorname{iteratedDeriv}(n+1,f)(\\xi)\\,\\frac{(x-x_0)^{\\,n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\\]Here $T_n(f;[x_0,x],x_0)(x)$ denotes the evaluation at $x$ of the Taylor polynomial of order $n$ for $f$ on $[x_0,x]$, and $\\operatorname{iteratedDeriv}(n+1,f)(\\xi)$ is the $(n+1)$‑st iterated derivative of $f$ within the interval evaluated at $\\xi$."
