      "full_name": "Asymptotics.IsBigO.hasFDerivAt",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: Asymptotics.IsBigO.hasFDerivAt | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {𝕜 : Type u_1} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField 𝕜] {E : Type u_2} [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup E]\n  [inst_2 : NormedSpace 𝕜 E] {F : Type u_3} [inst_3 : NormedAddCommGroup F] [inst_4 : NormedSpace 𝕜 F] {f : E → F}\n  {x₀ : E} {n : ℕ}, (f =O[nhds x₀] fun x => ‖x - x₀‖ ^ n) → 1 < n → HasFDerivAt f 0 x₀ | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Basic",
      "informal_statement": "Let $E$ and $F$ be normed spaces over a non-discrete normed field $\\mathbb{K}$, and let $f : E \\to F$ be a function. If $f(x) = O(\\|x - x_0\\|^n)$ as $x \\to x_0$ for some $n > 1$, then $f$ has Fréchet derivative $0$ at $x_0$."
