      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: Convex.isLittleO_alternate_sum_square | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {E : Type u_1} {F : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : NormedAddCommGroup F]\n  [inst_3 : NormedSpace ℝ F] {s : Set E},\n  Convex ℝ s →\n    ∀ {f : E → F} {f' : E → E →L[ℝ] F} {f'' : E →L[ℝ] E →L[ℝ] F},\n      (∀ x ∈ interior s, HasFDerivAt f (f' x) x) →\n        ∀ {x : E},\n          x ∈ s →\n            HasFDerivWithinAt f' f'' (interior s) x →\n              ∀ {v w : E},\n                x + 4 • v ∈ interior s →\n                  x + 4 • w ∈ interior s →\n                    (fun h =>\n                        f (x + h • (2 • v + 2 • w)) + f (x + h • (v + w)) - f (x + h • (2 • v + w)) -\n                            f (x + h • (v + 2 • w)) -\n                          h ^ 2 • (f'' v) w) =o[nhdsWithin 0 (Set.Ioi 0)]\n                      fun h => h ^ 2 | Path: Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Symmetric",
      "informal_statement": "Let $E$ be a real vector space and $s \\subseteq E$ a convex set with nonempty interior. Consider a function $f : E \\to F$ (where $F$ is another real vector space) that is differentiable in the interior of $s$, with derivative $f' : E \\to E \\toL[ℝ] F$. Suppose $f'' : E \\toL[ℝ] E \\toL[ℝ] F$ is the second derivative of $f$ at a point $x \\in s$ within the interior of $s$. \n\nFor any vectors $v, w \\in E$ such that $x + 4v$ and $x + 4w$ belong to the interior of $s$, the following asymptotic relation holds as $h \\to 0^+$:\n$$ f(x + h(2v + 2w)) + f(x + h(v + w)) - f(x + h(2v + w)) - f(x + h(v + 2w)) - h^2 f''(v)(w) = o(h^2). $$"
